IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc3-helpers`
IMPORT `ssc3-a-s43-s44`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4, ss 47 to 48C and the blank ss 49, 50 (part ssc3).
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- Increase of Category A retirement pension for invalidity (s 47); use of a former spouse's contributions (s 48);
-- Category B retirement pension for a married person or civil partner (s 48A), a divorcee or former civil partner
-- (s 48AA), a widow, widower or surviving civil partner (s 48B and s 48BB), and in general (s 48C).
--
-- The contributor (the spouse, the former spouse, the deceased) is a Person of the core: the sex, date of birth and
-- date of attaining pensionable age are facts. "Attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016" is a comparison of the
-- core's date with that day. Whether the contributor's contributions satisfy Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5 (the
-- conditions) or paragraph 5A (the condition) is another part's answer (seam S1), an input here; which of the two the
-- section points to is encoded here, with the type `s 44(1A) Contribution test` of ssc3-a-s43-s44.l4.

§ `Part II: Category A and Category B retirement pensions, increases and the use of another's contributions`

§§ `Section 47: increase of Category A retirement pension for invalidity`

-- (6): regulations may provide that the 8 weeks of (1) is a larger number of weeks.
-- src:1454 | (6) Regulations may provide that subsection (1) above shall have effect as if for the reference to 8 weeks there were substituted a reference to a larger number of weeks specified in the regulations.
@ref s 47(6) (src:1454)
GIVEN `a larger number of weeks specified in regulations` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(6) the number of weeks of subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a larger number of weeks specified in regulations`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 8
    WHEN JUST larger THEN max 8 larger

-- (1)(a): any day falling within the period of 8 weeks ending immediately before the day the pensioner attains
-- pensionable age.
-- src:1445 | (a) any day falling within the period of 8 weeks ending immediately before the day on which he attains pensionable age; or
@ref s 47(1)(a) (src:1445)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      day IS A DATE
      weeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 47(1)(a) the day falls within the period of weeks ending immediately before the day the pensioner attains pensionable age` MEANS
    day AT LEAST (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` MINUS (weeks TIMES 7))
    AND day LESS THAN pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age`

-- (1)(b): the last day before the beginning of that period.
-- src:1446 | (b) the last day before the beginning of that period;
@ref s 47(1)(b) (src:1446)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      weeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 47(1)(b) the last day before the beginning of the period` MEANS
    (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` MINUS (weeks TIMES 7)) MINUS 1

-- (1): "Subject to section 61 below, the weekly rate of a Category A retirement pension shall be increased if the
-- pensioner was entitled to an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit by virtue of regulations under section
-- 30B(7) in respect of (a) any day falling within the period or (b) the last day before the beginning of that period;
-- and the increase shall ... be of an amount equal to the appropriate weekly rate of the age addition ... on that day."
-- Section 61(1) (this part's range, answered by the caller) takes the increase away; section 30B(7) (ssc2) answers
-- the entitlement and the rate.
-- src:1444 | (1) Subject to section 61 below, the weekly rate of a Category A retirement pension shall be increased if the pensioner was entitled to an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit by virtue of regulations under section 30B(7) above in respect of—
-- src:1445 | (a) any day falling within the period of 8 weeks ending immediately before the day on which he attains pensionable age; or
-- src:1446 | (b) the last day before the beginning of that period;
-- src:1447 | and the increase shall, subject to subsection (2) below, be of an amount equal to the appropriate weekly rate of the age addition to long-term incapacity benefit by virtue of regulations under section 30B(7) above on that day.
@ref s 47(1) (src:1444-1447)
GIVEN `s 61(1) the increase under section 47(1) is excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 30B(7) the pensioner was entitled to an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit in respect of a day within the period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 30B(7) the pensioner was entitled to an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit in respect of the last day before the period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 30B(7) the weekly rate of the age addition in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 47(1) the increase of the weekly rate in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 61(1) the increase under section 47(1) is excluded`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): section 61(1), "shall not be increased under section 47(1) above"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `the increase apart from section 61`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the increase apart from section 61` EQUALS JUST 0
        THEN JUST 0
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 61 takes the increase away is that section's answer, which the caller has not given
    WHERE
        `the entitled period` MEANS
            `ssc3 helper any of`
                (LIST
                    `s 30B(7) the pensioner was entitled to an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit in respect of a day within the period`
                  , `s 30B(7) the pensioner was entitled to an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit in respect of the last day before the period`)
        `the increase apart from section 61` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the entitled period`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 30B(7) the weekly rate of the age addition in pounds`
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the weekly rate of a Category A retirement pension shall be increased if the pensioner was entitled to an age addition" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the age addition was payable is section 30B(7)'s answer (ssc2)

-- (3A): references to additional pension in (2) and (3) do not include any amount attributable to units of additional pension.
-- src:1450 | (3A) In subsections (2) and (3) above references to additional pension do not include any amount of additional pension attributable to units of additional pension.
@ref s 47(3A) (src:1450)
GIVEN `the additional pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of it attributable to units of additional pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(3A) the additional pension for subsections (2) and (3) in pounds` MEANS
    `the additional pension in pounds` MINUS `the amount of it attributable to units of additional pension in pounds`

-- (4): the additional pension is that pension after any increase under section 52(3) but without any increase under
-- paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5.
-- src:1452 | (4) In this section any reference to an additional pension is a reference to that pension after any increase under section 52(3) below but without any increase under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5 to this Act.
@ref s 47(4) (src:1452)
GIVEN `the additional pension including any increase under section 52(3) and any increase under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5 in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the increase under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5 in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(4) the additional pension in pounds` MEANS
    `the additional pension including any increase under section 52(3) and any increase under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5 in pounds`
    MINUS `the increase under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5 in pounds`

-- (3): the "relevant amount" is the additional pension reduced by any reduction in the weekly rate made by virtue of
-- section 46 of the Pensions Act (the amount of the reduction is an input).
-- src:1449 | (3) In subsection (2) above the “relevant amount” means an amount equal to the additional pension, reduced by the amount of any reduction in the weekly rate of the Category A retirement pension made by virtue of section 46 of the Pensions Act.
@ref s 47(3) (src:1449)
GIVEN `the additional pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction in the weekly rate made by virtue of section 46 of the Pensions Act in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(3) the relevant amount in pounds` MEANS
    `the additional pension in pounds` MINUS `the reduction in the weekly rate made by virtue of section 46 of the Pensions Act in pounds`

-- (2): where the weekly rate includes an additional pension, the relevant amount is deducted from the increase, and the
-- pensioner is entitled to an increase "only if there is a balance remaining after that deduction" (of that balance).
-- src:1448 | (2) Where for any period the weekly rate of a Category A retirement pension includes an additional pension, for that period the relevant amount shall be deducted from the amount that would otherwise be the increase under subsection (1) above and the pensioner shall be entitled to an increase under that subsection only if there is a balance remaining after that deduction and, if there is such a balance, of an amount equal to it.
@ref s 47(2) (src:1448)
GIVEN `the increase under subsection (1) in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate of the pension includes an additional pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(2) the increase after the deduction in pounds` MEANS
    IF NOT `the weekly rate of the pension includes an additional pension`
    THEN `the increase under subsection (1) in pounds`
    ELSE
        IF `the increase under subsection (1) in pounds` GREATER THAN `the relevant amount in pounds`
        THEN `the increase under subsection (1) in pounds` MINUS `the relevant amount in pounds`
        ELSE 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the pensioner shall be entitled to an increase under that subsection only if there is a balance remaining after that deduction"

-- (5): in ascertaining the rate of the age addition regard is had to the rates in force from time to time.
-- src:1453 | (5) In ascertaining for the purposes of subsection (1) above the rate of a pensioner’s age addition to long-term incapacity benefit by virtue of regulations under section 30B(7) above, regard shall be had to the rates in force from time to time.
@ref s 47(5) (src:1453)
GIVEN `the rate of the age addition in force on the day in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 47(5) the rate of the age addition in pounds` MEANS `the rate of the age addition in force on the day in pounds`

§§ `Section 48: use of former spouse's contributions`

DECLARE `s 48(4) Kind of relationship` IS ONE OF
    `s 48(4) a marriage`
    `s 48(4) a civil partnership`
    `s 48(4) a relationship of another kind`

-- (4): "relevant relationship" means a marriage or civil partnership.
-- src:1463 | (4) In this section, “relevant relationship” means a marriage or civil partnership.
@ref s 48(4) (src:1463)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 48(4) Kind of relationship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(4) the relationship is a relevant relationship` MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `s 48(4) a marriage` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 48(4) a civil partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 48(4) a relationship of another kind` THEN FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"relevant relationship\" means a marriage or civil partnership"

-- (3): where a person has been in a relevant relationship more than once, the section applies only to the last one.
-- src:1462 | (3) Where a person has been in a relevant relationship more than once, this section applies only to the last relevant relationship and the references to his relevant relationship and his former spouse or civil partner shall be construed accordingly.
@ref s 48(3) (src:1462)
GIVEN `it is the last relevant relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(3) the relationship is not excluded by subsection (3)` MEANS `it is the last relevant relationship`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section applies only to the last relevant relationship"

-- (2): subsection (1) shall not apply to a person who attained pensionable age before 6 April 1979 if the termination
-- of the relevant relationship also occurred before that date.
-- src:1460 | (2) Subsection (1) above shall not apply in relation to any person who attained pensionable age before 6th April 1979 if the termination of his relevant relationship also occurred before that date.
@ref s 48(2) (src:1460)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `the relevant relationship terminated on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(2) subsection (1) is disapplied for the person` MEANS
    pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1979)
    AND `the relevant relationship terminated on` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1979)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not apply ... if the termination of his relevant relationship also occurred before that date" -- a failed "if" counts as no disapplication (marginal reading (a))

-- (2A): regulations under (1) may not provide for contributions in respect of times on or after 6 April 2016 to be
-- treated as another person's.
-- src:1461 | (2A) Regulations under subsection (1) may not provide for contributions of a person in respect of times on or after 6 April 2016 to be treated as contributions of another person.
@ref s 48(2A) (src:1461)
GIVEN `the time to which the contributions relate` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(2A) regulations under subsection (1) may provide for contributions in respect of the time to be treated as another person's` MEANS
    IF `the time to which the contributions relate` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 2016)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Regulations under subsection (1) may not provide for contributions of a person in respect of times on or after 6 April 2016 to be treated as contributions of another person"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): earlier times are for the regulations

-- (1): where a person who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 (a) has been in a relevant relationship and (b)
-- does not, in respect of the tax year in which it terminated or any previous tax year, satisfy with their own
-- contributions the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension, the former spouse's or civil
-- partner's contributions "may to the prescribed extent be treated as if they were his own contributions" -- "but only
-- in respect of any claim for a Category A retirement pension". The prescribed extent is for the regulations; this
-- answers whether the contributions may be so treated at all.
-- src:1456 | (1) Where a person who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016—
-- src:1457 | (a) has been in a relevant relationship, and
-- src:1458 | (b) in respect of the tax year in which the relationship terminated or any previous tax year, does not with his own contributions satisfy the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension,
-- src:1459 | then, for the purpose of enabling him to satisfy those conditions (but only in respect of any claim for a Category A retirement pension), the contributions of his former spouse or civil partner may to the prescribed extent be treated as if they were his own contributions.
@ref s 48(1) (src:1456-1459)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `the person has been in a relevant relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension are satisfied by the person's own contributions in respect of the tax year in which the relationship terminated or any previous tax year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claim is a claim for a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 48(2) subsection (1) is disapplied for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 48(3) the relationship is not excluded by subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(1) the former spouse's or civil partner's contributions may be treated as the person's own` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the claim is a claim for a Category A retirement pension` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only in respect of any claim for a Category A retirement pension"
        IF `s 48(2) subsection (1) is disapplied for the person` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) above shall not apply" (s 48(2))
        IF NOT `s 48(3) the relationship is not excluded by subsection (3)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section applies only to the last relevant relationship" (s 48(3))
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 -- (a) has been in a relevant relationship, and (b) ... does not with his own contributions satisfy the contribution conditions" -- a failed "where" is read like a failed "if" (marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md)
            `ssc3 helper all of`
                (LIST
                    JUST (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
                  , JUST `the person has been in a relevant relationship`
                  , `ssc3 helper not` `sch 3 pt I the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension are satisfied by the person's own contributions in respect of the tax year in which the relationship terminated or any previous tax year`)

-- (5): a civil partnership is not to be treated as having terminated by reason of its having been (a) converted into a
-- marriage under section 9 of the Marriage (Same Sex Couples) Act 2013 or the 2020 or 2014 regulations named, (b)
-- changed into a marriage under the Marriage (Scotland) Act 1977, (c) changed into a marriage under section 10 of the
-- Marriage and Civil Partnership (Scotland) Act 2014, or (d) changed into a marriage under Part 5 of that Act and the
-- Civil Partnership Act 2004 (Consequential Provisions and Modifications) Order 2014.
-- The text carries two versions of subsection (5): the first (src:1464) is the single sentence naming only the
-- conversion in (a); the second (src:1465-1469) adds (b) to (d). The second contains the first and is encoded.
DECLARE `s 48(5) How the civil partnership ended` IS ONE OF
    `s 48(5)(a) converted into a marriage under a conversion enactment named in paragraph (a)`
    `s 48(5)(b) changed into a marriage under the Marriage (Scotland) Act 1977`
    `s 48(5)(c) changed into a marriage in accordance with provision made under section 10 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Scotland) Act 2014`
    `s 48(5)(d) changed into a marriage under Part 5 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Scotland) Act 2014 and Civil Partnership Act 2004 (Consequential Provisions and Modifications) Order 2014`
    `s 48(5) ended in some other way`

-- src:1465 | (5) For the purposes of this section, a civil partnership is not to be treated as having terminated by reason of its having been—
-- src:1466 | (a) converted into a marriage under section 9 of the Marriage (Same Sex Couples) Act 2013 or Part 3 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020 or Part 3 or 4 of the Marriage of Same Sex Couples (Conversion of Civil Partnership) Regulations 2014;
-- src:1467 | (b) changed into a marriage under the Marriage (Scotland) Act 1977;
-- src:1468 | (c) changed into a marriage in accordance with provision made under section 10 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Scotland) Act 2014; or
-- src:1469 | (d) changed into a marriage under Part 5 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Scotland) Act 2014 and Civil Partnership Act 2004 (Consequential Provisions and Modifications) Order 2014.
@ref s 48(5) (src:1465-1469)
GIVEN how IS A `s 48(5) How the civil partnership ended`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(5) the civil partnership is treated as having terminated` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `s 48(5) ended in some other way` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names four ways of ending that do not count as termination, and says nothing of any other
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a civil partnership is not to be treated as having terminated by reason of its having been"

-- src:1464 | (5) For the purposes of this section, a civil partnership is not to be treated as having terminated by reason of its having been converted into a marriage under section 9 of the Marriage (Same Sex Couples) Act 2013 or Part 3 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020 or Part 3 or 4 of the Marriage of Same Sex Couples (Conversion of Civil Partnership) Regulations 2014.
@ref s 48(5), first version (src:1464)
GIVEN `the civil partnership was converted into a marriage under section 9 of the Marriage (Same Sex Couples) Act 2013 or Part 3 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020 or Part 3 or 4 of the Marriage of Same Sex Couples (Conversion of Civil Partnership) Regulations 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(5) first version: the civil partnership is treated as having terminated by reason of the conversion` MEANS
    IF `the civil partnership was converted into a marriage under section 9 of the Marriage (Same Sex Couples) Act 2013 or Part 3 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020 or Part 3 or 4 of the Marriage of Same Sex Couples (Conversion of Civil Partnership) Regulations 2014`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a civil partnership is not to be treated as having terminated by reason of its having been converted into a marriage"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence speaks of the conversion only

-- (6): a marriage is not to be treated as having terminated by reason of its having been converted into a civil
-- partnership under Part 3, 4 or 5 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020.
-- src:1470 | (6) For the purposes of this section, a marriage is not to be treated as having terminated by reason of its having been converted into a civil partnership under Part 3, 4 or 5 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020.
@ref s 48(6) (src:1470)
GIVEN `the marriage was converted into a civil partnership under Part 3, 4 or 5 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(6) the marriage is treated as having terminated` MEANS
    IF `the marriage was converted into a civil partnership under Part 3, 4 or 5 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a marriage is not to be treated as having terminated by reason of its having been converted into a civil partnership"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of that conversion only

§§ `Section 48A: Category B retirement pension for married person or civil partner`

-- (6): the relevant contribution condition is (a) the conditions in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 where the spouse was
-- born before 6 April 1945, (b) in any other case the condition in paragraph 5A.
-- src:1490 | (6) In subsection (1)(b)(ii) “the relevant contribution condition” means—
-- src:1491 | (a) in a case where the spouse was born before 6 April 1945, the conditions in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3;
-- src:1492 | (b) in any other case, the condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3.
@ref s 48A(6) (src:1490-1492)
GIVEN spouse IS A Person
GIVETH A `s 44(1A) Contribution test`
`s 48A(6) the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
    IF spouse's `date of birth` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1945)
    THEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5`
    ELSE `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A`

-- (2): subsection (1) does not confer a right to a Category B retirement pension on (a) a man whose spouse was born
-- before 6 April 1950 or (b) a woman whose wife was born before 6 April 1950. Section 51ZA(1) says paragraph (b) does
-- not prevent a woman from being entitled where her spouse is a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition
-- certificate and the marriage subsisted before it was issued.
-- src:1477 | (2) But subsection (1) does not confer a right to a Category B retirement pension on—
-- src:1478 | (a) a man whose spouse was born before 6 April 1950, or
-- src:1479 | (b) a woman whose wife was born before 6 April 1950.
@ref s 48A(2) (src:1477-1479)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      spouse IS A Person
      `s 51ZA(1) section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(2) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF person's `sex` EQUALS Man AND spouse's `date of birth` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1950)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF person's `sex` EQUALS Woman AND spouse's `sex` EQUALS Woman AND spouse's `date of birth` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1950)
        THEN
            CONSIDER `s 51ZA(1) section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): section 51ZA(1), "Section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent a woman from being entitled"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the gender-recognition facts of section 51ZA(1) hold is that section's answer
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is stated for "(a) a man ... or (b) a woman ..." and for no one else (a closed list)

-- (1): a married person is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the spouse's contributions if
-- (a) the person attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and (b) the spouse (i) has attained pensionable age and
-- (ii) satisfies the relevant contribution condition (subsection (6)). Subsection (2) is a bar on (1).
-- src:1472 | (1) A married person is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her spouse if—
-- src:1473 | (a) the person attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1474 | (b) the spouse—
-- src:1475 | (i) has attained pensionable age, and
-- src:1476 | (ii) satisfies the relevant contribution condition.
@ref s 48A(1) (src:1472-1476)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      spouse IS A Person
      `the person is married to the spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
      `s 51ZA(1) section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(1) the married person is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the spouse's contributions` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A married person is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her spouse if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a)); and "But subsection (1) does not confer a right" (s 48A(2))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            `ssc3 helper not` (`s 48A(2) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` person spouse `s 51ZA(1) section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled`)
          , JUST `the person is married to the spouse`
          , JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , JUST (spouse's `date of attaining pensionable age` AT MOST day)
          , `the spouse satisfies the relevant contribution condition`)
    WHERE
        `the spouse satisfies the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 48A(6) the relevant contribution condition` spouse
            WHEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor`
            WHEN `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor`

-- (3): a civil partner is entitled by virtue of the contributions of the contributing civil partner if (a) the person
-- attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and (b) the contributing civil partner (i) was born on or after
-- 6 April 1950, (ii) has attained pensionable age and (iii) satisfies the condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3.
-- src:1480 | (3) A person who is a civil partner is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her civil partner (“the contributing civil partner”) if—
-- src:1481 | (a) the person attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1482 | (b) the contributing civil partner—
-- src:1483 | (i) was born on or after 6 April 1950,
-- src:1484 | (ii) has attained pensionable age, and
-- src:1485 | (iii) satisfies the condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3.
@ref s 48A(3) (src:1480-1485)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `the contributing civil partner` IS A Person
      `the person is the civil partner of the contributing civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
      `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(3) the civil partner is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the contributing civil partner` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who is a civil partner is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her civil partner (\"the contributing civil partner\") if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST `the person is the civil partner of the contributing civil partner`
          , JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , JUST (`the contributing civil partner`'s `date of birth` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 1950))
          , JUST (`the contributing civil partner`'s `date of attaining pensionable age` AT MOST day)
          , `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor`)

-- (4): the weekly rate is that specified in paragraph 5 of Part 1 of Schedule 4 (the table is omitted from this text: an input).
-- src:1486 | (4) A Category B retirement pension payable under this section is payable at the weekly rate specified in paragraph 5 of Part 1 of Schedule 4.
@ref s 48A(4) (src:1486)
GIVEN `sch 4 pt I para 5 the weekly rate of a Category B retirement pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 48A(4) the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds` MEANS `sch 4 pt I para 5 the weekly rate of a Category B retirement pension in pounds`

-- (5): a person ceases to be entitled if (a) the spouse or civil partner dies or (b) the person otherwise ceases to be
-- married or in the civil partnership. ((6A) and (6B) say what is not to be treated as ceasing.)
-- src:1487 | (5) A person ceases to be entitled to a Category B retirement pension under this section if—
-- src:1488 | (a) the person's spouse or civil partner dies (but see sections 48B and 51), or
-- src:1489 | (b) the person otherwise ceases to be married or in the civil partnership (but see section 48AA).
@ref s 48A(5) (src:1487-1489)
GIVEN `the spouse or civil partner dies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person otherwise ceases to be married or in the civil partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(5) the person ceases to be entitled to the Category B retirement pension under section 48A` MEANS
    IF `the spouse or civil partner dies` OR `the person otherwise ceases to be married or in the civil partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person ceases to be entitled to a Category B retirement pension under this section if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))

-- (6A): for (5)(b), a person is not to be treated as having ceased to be in a civil partnership by reason of its having
-- been converted into a marriage under (a) Part 3 of the 2020 Northern Ireland regulations or (b) Part 3 or 4 of the
-- 2014 regulations where the civil partnership is a convertible Northern Ireland civil partnership.
-- src:1493 | (6A) For the purposes of subsection (5)(b), a person is not to be treated as having ceased to be in a civil partnership by reason of its having been converted into a marriage under—
-- src:1494 | (a) Part 3 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020, or
-- src:1495 | (b) Part 3 or 4 of the Marriage of Same Sex Couples (Conversion of Civil Partnership) Regulations 2014 where the civil partnership is a convertible Northern Ireland civil partnership as defined by regulation 2 of those Regulations.
@ref s 48A(6A) (src:1493-1495)
GIVEN `the civil partnership was converted into a marriage under a provision named in subsection (6A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(6A) the person is treated as having ceased to be in a civil partnership` MEANS
    IF `the civil partnership was converted into a marriage under a provision named in subsection (6A)`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is not to be treated as having ceased to be in a civil partnership by reason of its having been converted into a marriage"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of those conversions only

-- (6B): for (5)(b), a person is not to be treated as having ceased to be married by reason of the marriage having been
-- converted into a civil partnership under Part 3, 4 or 5 of the 2020 Northern Ireland regulations.
-- src:1496 | (6B) For the purposes of subsection (5)(b), a person is not to be treated as having ceased to be married by reason of the person’s marriage having been converted into a civil partnership under Part 3, 4 or 5 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020.
@ref s 48A(6B) (src:1496)
GIVEN `the marriage was converted into a civil partnership under Part 3, 4 or 5 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(6B) the person is treated as having ceased to be married` MEANS
    IF `the marriage was converted into a civil partnership under Part 3, 4 or 5 of the Marriage and Civil Partnership (Northern Ireland) (No. 2) Regulations 2020`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is not to be treated as having ceased to be married by reason of the person's marriage having been converted into a civil partnership"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of that conversion only

-- (7): no account is to be taken of the spouse's or contributing civil partner's earnings factors for the tax year
-- beginning with 6 April 2016 or any later tax year.
-- src:1497 | (7) For the purposes of any provision of this Act as it applies in relation to this section, no account is to be taken of any earnings factors of the spouse or contributing civil partner for the tax year beginning with 6 April 2016 or any later tax year.
@ref s 48A(7) (src:1497)
GIVEN year IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(7) the earnings factor of the spouse or contributing civil partner for the tax year is taken into account` MEANS
    IF year's `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 2016
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no account is to be taken of any earnings factors of the spouse or contributing civil partner for the tax year beginning with 6 April 2016 or any later tax year"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): earlier years are left to the other provisions

§§ `Section 48AA: Category B retirement pension for divorcee or former civil partner`

-- (6): as s 48A(6), for the former spouse (paragraph 5 where born before 6 April 1945, else paragraph 5A).
-- src:1520 | (6) In subsection (1)(b)(ii) “the relevant contribution condition” means—
-- src:1521 | (a) in a case where the former spouse was born before 6 April 1945, the conditions in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3;
-- src:1522 | (b) in any other case, the condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3.
@ref s 48AA(6) (src:1520-1522)
GIVEN `former spouse` IS A Person
GIVETH A `s 44(1A) Contribution test`
`s 48AA(6) the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
    IF `former spouse`'s `date of birth` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1945)
    THEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5`
    ELSE `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A`

-- (2): subsection (1) does not confer a right on (a) a man whose former spouse was born before 6 April 1950 or (b) a
-- woman whose former wife was born before 6 April 1950. Section 51ZA(2) says paragraph (b) does not prevent a woman
-- from being entitled where her former spouse was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate at the
-- time of dissolution and the marriage subsisted before it was issued.
-- src:1507 | (2) But subsection (1) does not confer a right to a Category B retirement pension on—
-- src:1508 | (a) a man whose former spouse was born before 6 April 1950, or
-- src:1509 | (b) a woman whose former wife was born before 6 April 1950.
@ref s 48AA(2) (src:1507-1509)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `former spouse` IS A Person
      `s 51ZA(2) section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48AA(2) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF person's `sex` EQUALS Man AND `former spouse`'s `date of birth` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1950)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF person's `sex` EQUALS Woman AND `former spouse`'s `sex` EQUALS Woman AND `former spouse`'s `date of birth` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1950)
        THEN
            CONSIDER `s 51ZA(2) section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): section 51ZA(2), "Section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent a woman from being entitled"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the gender-recognition facts of section 51ZA(2) hold is that section's answer
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is stated for "(a) a man ... or (b) a woman ..." and for no one else (a closed list)

-- (1): a person whose marriage has been dissolved is entitled by virtue of the former spouse's contributions if (a) the
-- person attained pensionable age (i) before 6 April 2016 and (ii) before the marriage was dissolved, and (b) the former
-- spouse (i) attained pensionable age before the marriage was dissolved and (ii) satisfied the relevant contribution
-- condition. Subsection (2) is a bar on (1).
-- src:1500 | (1) A person who has been in a marriage that has been dissolved is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her former spouse if—
-- src:1501 | (a) the person attained pensionable age—
-- src:1502 | (i) before 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1503 | (ii) before the marriage was dissolved, and
-- src:1504 | (b) the former spouse—
-- src:1505 | (i) attained pensionable age before the marriage was dissolved, and
-- src:1506 | (ii) satisfied the relevant contribution condition.
@ref s 48AA(1) (src:1500-1506)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `former spouse` IS A Person
      `the marriage was dissolved on` IS A DATE
      `s 51ZA(2) section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48AA(1) the person whose marriage has been dissolved is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the former spouse's contributions` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who has been in a marriage that has been dissolved is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her former spouse if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a)); and "But subsection (1) does not confer a right" (s 48AA(2))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            `ssc3 helper not` (`s 48AA(2) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` person `former spouse` `s 51ZA(2) section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled`)
          , JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN `the marriage was dissolved on`)
          , JUST (`former spouse`'s `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN `the marriage was dissolved on`)
          , `the former spouse satisfied the relevant contribution condition`)
    WHERE
        `the former spouse satisfied the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 48AA(6) the relevant contribution condition` `former spouse`
            WHEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor`
            WHEN `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor`

-- (3): a person whose civil partnership has been dissolved is entitled by virtue of the former civil partner's
-- contributions if (a) the person attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and before the dissolution and (b) the
-- former civil partner (i) was born on or after 6 April 1950, (ii) attained pensionable age before the dissolution and
-- (iii) satisfied the condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3.
-- src:1510 | (3) A person who has been in a civil partnership that has been dissolved is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her former civil partner if—
-- src:1511 | (a) the person attained pensionable age—
-- src:1512 | (i) before 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1513 | (ii) before the civil partnership was dissolved, and
-- src:1514 | (b) the former civil partner—
-- src:1515 | (i) was born on or after 6 April 1950,
-- src:1516 | (ii) attained pensionable age before the civil partnership was dissolved, and
-- src:1517 | (iii) satisfied the condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3.
@ref s 48AA(3) (src:1510-1517)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `former civil partner` IS A Person
      `the civil partnership was dissolved on` IS A DATE
      `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48AA(3) the person whose civil partnership has been dissolved is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the former civil partner's contributions` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who has been in a civil partnership that has been dissolved is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her former civil partner if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN `the civil partnership was dissolved on`)
          , JUST (`former civil partner`'s `date of birth` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 1950))
          , JUST (`former civil partner`'s `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN `the civil partnership was dissolved on`)
          , `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor`)

-- (4) and (5): the weekly rate while the former spouse or civil partner is alive is that in paragraph 5 of Part 1 of
-- Schedule 4 (an input); after the former spouse or civil partner is dead it is the weekly rate of the basic pension in
-- section 44(4).
-- src:1518 | (4) During any period when the person's former spouse or civil partner is alive, a Category B retirement pension payable under this section is payable at the weekly rate specified in paragraph 5 of Part 1 of Schedule 4.
-- src:1519 | (5) During any period after the person's former spouse or civil partner is dead, a Category B retirement pension payable under this section is payable at the weekly rate of the basic pension specified in section 44(4).
@ref s 48AA(4) and (5) (src:1518-1519)
GIVEN `the former spouse or civil partner is alive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 4 pt I para 5 the weekly rate of a Category B retirement pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 48AA(4) the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the former spouse or civil partner is alive`
    THEN `sch 4 pt I para 5 the weekly rate of a Category B retirement pension in pounds`
    ELSE `s 44(4) the weekly rate of the basic pension in pounds` FALSE

-- (7): no account of the former spouse's or civil partner's earnings factors for 2016-17 or any later tax year.
-- src:1523 | (7) For the purposes of any provision of this Act as it applies in relation to this section, no account is to be taken of any earnings factors of the former spouse or civil partner for the tax year beginning with 6 April 2016 or any later tax year.
@ref s 48AA(7) (src:1523)
GIVEN year IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48AA(7) the earnings factor of the former spouse or civil partner for the tax year is taken into account` MEANS
    IF year's `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 2016
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no account is to be taken of any earnings factors of the former spouse or civil partner for the tax year beginning with 6 April 2016 or any later tax year"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): earlier years are left to the other provisions

-- (8): a voidable marriage or civil partnership which has been annulled is treated for this section as if it had been a
-- valid marriage or civil partnership dissolved at the date of annulment.
-- src:1524 | (8) A voidable marriage or civil partnership which has been annulled is to be treated for the purposes of this section as if it had been a valid marriage or civil partnership which was dissolved at the date of annulment.
@ref s 48AA(8) (src:1524)
GIVEN `the marriage or civil partnership was voidable and has been annulled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of annulment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 48AA(8) the date on which the marriage or civil partnership is treated as dissolved` MEANS
    IF `the marriage or civil partnership was voidable and has been annulled`
    THEN JUST `the date of annulment`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a voidable marriage or civil partnership which has been annulled"

§§ `Section 48B: Category B retirement pension for widows and widowers`

-- (1ZB): the relevant contribution condition for a spouse who died: (a) the conditions in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3
-- where the spouse (i) died before 6 April 2010 or (ii) died on or after that date having attained pensionable age
-- before that date; (b) in any other case the condition in paragraph 5A. In the gender-change case of section 51ZA(3)
-- the reference in (a)(ii) to the spouse having attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010 is read as a reference to
-- the spouse having been born before 6 April 1945.
-- src:1535 | (1ZB) In subsection (1)(b) “the relevant contribution condition” means—
-- src:1536 | (a) in a case where the spouse—
-- src:1537 | (i) died before 6 April 2010, or
-- src:1538 | (ii) died on or after that date having attained pensionable age before that date,
-- src:1539 | the conditions in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3, and
-- src:1540 | (b) in any other case, the condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3.
@ref s 48B(1ZB) (src:1535-1540)
GIVEN spouse IS A Person
      `the spouse died on` IS A DATE
      `s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 44(1A) Contribution test`
`s 48B(1ZB) the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
    IF `the spouse died on` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2010)
    THEN JUST `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5`
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
            JUST (IF spouse's `date of birth` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 1945)
                  THEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5`
                  ELSE `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A`)
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
            JUST (IF spouse's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2010)
                  THEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5`
                  ELSE `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the gender-recognition facts of section 51ZA(3) hold decides which reading of (a)(ii) applies, and that is that section's answer

-- (1ZA): subsection (1) does not confer a right on (a) a man who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010 or (b) a
-- woman who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010 and whose spouse was a woman. Section 51ZA(3) says paragraph
-- (b) does not prevent a woman from being entitled where her dead spouse was, at the time of death, a woman by virtue
-- of a full gender recognition certificate and the marriage subsisted before it was issued.
-- src:1532 | (1ZA) But subsection (1) does not confer a right to a Category B retirement pension on—
-- src:1533 | (a) a man who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010, or
-- src:1534 | (b) a woman who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010 and whose spouse was a woman.
@ref s 48B(1ZA) (src:1532-1534)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      spouse IS A Person
      `s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(1ZA) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF person's `sex` EQUALS Man AND person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2010)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF person's `sex` EQUALS Woman AND spouse's `sex` EQUALS Woman AND person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2010)
        THEN
            CONSIDER `s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): section 51ZA(3), "Section 48B(1ZA)(b) does not prevent a woman from being entitled"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the gender-recognition facts of section 51ZA(3) hold is that section's answer
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is stated for "(a) a man ... or (b) a woman ..." and for no one else (a closed list)

-- (1): a person whose spouse died while they were married is entitled by virtue of the spouse's contributions if (a) the
-- pensioner attained pensionable age (i) before 6 April 2016 and (ii) before the spouse died and (b) the spouse satisfied
-- the relevant contribution condition (1ZB). Subsection (1ZA) is a bar on (1).
-- src:1527 | (1) A person (“the pensioner”) whose spouse died while they were married is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her spouse if—
-- src:1528 | (a) the pensioner attained pensionable age—
-- src:1529 | (i) before 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1530 | (ii) before the spouse died, and
-- src:1531 | (b) the spouse satisfied the relevant contribution condition.
@ref s 48B(1) (src:1527-1531)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      spouse IS A Person
      `the spouse died on` IS A DATE
      `the spouse died while they were married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the spouse's contributions` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person (\"the pensioner\") whose spouse died while they were married is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her spouse if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a)); and "But subsection (1) does not confer a right" (s 48B(1ZA))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            `ssc3 helper not` (`s 48B(1ZA) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` person spouse `s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies`)
          , JUST `the spouse died while they were married`
          , JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN `the spouse died on`)
          , `the spouse satisfied the relevant contribution condition`)
    WHERE
        `the spouse satisfied the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 48B(1ZB) the relevant contribution condition` spouse `the spouse died on` `s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): see section 48B(1ZB)
            WHEN JUST `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor`
            WHEN JUST `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor`

-- (1B): the relevant contribution condition for a deceased civil partner: (a) paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 where the
-- deceased attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010; (b) in any other case paragraph 5A.
-- src:1546 | (1B) In subsection (1A)(b) “the relevant contribution condition” means—
-- src:1547 | (a) in a case where the deceased civil partner attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010, the conditions in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3, and
-- src:1548 | (b) in any other case, the condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3.
@ref s 48B(1B) (src:1546-1548)
GIVEN `deceased civil partner` IS A Person
GIVETH A `s 44(1A) Contribution test`
`s 48B(1B) the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
    IF `deceased civil partner`'s `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2010)
    THEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5`
    ELSE `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A`

-- (1A): a person whose civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other is entitled by virtue of the
-- civil partner's contributions if (a) the pensioner attained pensionable age (i) on or after 6 April 2010 but before 6
-- April 2016 and (ii) before the civil partner died and (b) the civil partner satisfied the relevant contribution condition (1B).
-- src:1541 | (1A) A person (“the pensioner”) whose civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her civil partner if—
-- src:1542 | (a) the pensioner attained pensionable age—
-- src:1543 | (i) on or after 6 April 2010 but before 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1544 | (ii) before the civil partner died, and
-- src:1545 | (b) the civil partner satisfied the relevant contribution condition.
@ref s 48B(1A) (src:1541-1545)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `deceased civil partner` IS A Person
      `the civil partner died on` IS A DATE
      `the civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(1A) the person whose civil partner died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the civil partner's contributions` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person (\"the pensioner\") whose civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his or her civil partner if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST `the civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other`
          , JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 2010))
          , JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , JUST (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN `the civil partner died on`)
          , `the civil partner satisfied the relevant contribution condition`)
    WHERE
        `the civil partner satisfied the relevant contribution condition` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 48B(1B) the relevant contribution condition` `deceased civil partner`
            WHEN `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a retirement pension are satisfied by the contributor`
            WHEN `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A` THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution condition for a retirement pension is satisfied by the contributor`

-- (3): where the spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age, references to the tax year in which the pensioner
-- attained pensionable age are taken as references to the tax year in which the spouse or civil partner died.
-- src:1553 | (3) Where the spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age, references in the provisions of sections 44 to 45B above and Schedule 4A below as applied by subsection (2) above to the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age shall be taken as references to the tax year in which the spouse or civil partner died.
@ref s 48B(3) (src:1553)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `the spouse or civil partner died on` IS A DATE
      `the spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 48B(3) the tax year taken as the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age` MEANS
    IF `the spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age`
    THEN `Tax year` OF (`ssc3 helper tax year of` `the spouse or civil partner died on`)
    ELSE `Tax year` OF (`ssc3 helper tax year of` (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age`))

-- (3A): no account of the deceased's earnings factors for the tax year beginning 6 April 2016 or later.
-- src:1554 | (3A) For the purposes of any provision of this Act as it applies in relation to this section, no account is to be taken of any earnings factors of the deceased for the tax year beginning with 6 April 2016 or any later tax year.
@ref s 48B(3A) (src:1554)
GIVEN year IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(3A) the earnings factor of the deceased for the tax year is taken into account` MEANS
    IF year's `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 2016
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no account is to be taken of any earnings factors of the deceased for the tax year beginning with 6 April 2016 or any later tax year"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): earlier years are left to the other provisions

-- (2): the weekly rate is the weekly rate of the basic pension plus half of the weekly rate of the additional pension,
-- both determined under ss 44 to 45B and Schedules 4A and 4B as for a Category A retirement pension; section 48C(3)
-- omits "half of" where the spouse died on or before 5 October 2002. The two rates arrive as inputs (the caller
-- computes them with `s 44(4)` and `s 45`).
-- src:1549 | (2) A Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of subsection (1) or (1A) above shall be payable at a weekly rate corresponding to—
-- src:1550 | (a) the weekly rate of the basic pension, plus
-- src:1551 | (b) half of the weekly rate of the additional pension,
-- src:1552 | determined in accordance with the provisions of sections 44 to 45B above and Schedules 4A and 4B below as they apply in relation to a Category A retirement pension, but subject to section 46 above and the modifications in subsection (3) below and section 48C(4) below.
@ref s 48B(2) (src:1549-1552)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the basic pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the weekly rate of the additional pension determined as for a Category A retirement pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `s 48C(3) the words "half of" are omitted from section 48B(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 48B(2) the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds` MEANS
    `ssc3 helper sum of`
        (LIST
            `the weekly rate of the basic pension in pounds`
          , CONSIDER `the weekly rate of the additional pension determined as for a Category A retirement pension in pounds`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST additional THEN
                IF `s 48C(3) the words "half of" are omitted from section 48B(2)(b)`
                THEN JUST additional
                ELSE JUST (additional DIVIDED BY 2))

-- (11) and (10): where the pensioner is entitled under (1) or (1A) and the spouse or civil partner attained pensionable
-- age on or after 6 April 2016 and died after attaining it, the additional pension determined under (2) is increased by
-- the percentage by which it would have increased under orders under section 150 of the Administration Act from the
-- date pensionable age was reached to the death. The percentage arrives as an input; it is applied as a multiplier of
-- (1 + the percentage / 100) (fork F6, see NOTES.md).
-- src:1570 | (10) Subsection (11) applies in the case of a pensioner entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of subsection (1) or (1A) whose spouse or civil partner—
-- src:1571 | (a) attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1572 | (b) died after attaining pensionable age.
-- src:1573 | (11) Where this subsection applies, the amount determined in accordance with subsection (2) as the weekly rate of the additional pension payable to the pensioner must be increased by such percentage as equals the overall percentage by which, had the pension been in payment as from the date when the spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age until the spouse’s or civil partner’s death, that weekly rate would have increased during that period by virtue of orders under section 150 of the Administration Act (annual uprating of benefits).
@ref s 48B(10) and (11) (src:1570-1573)
GIVEN `the spouse or civil partner attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the spouse or civil partner died after attaining pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of the additional pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the overall percentage by which the weekly rate would have increased by virtue of orders under section 150 of the Administration Act` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 48B(11) the weekly rate of the additional pension after the increase in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the spouse or civil partner attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2016` AND `the spouse or civil partner died after attaining pensionable age`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the overall percentage by which the weekly rate would have increased by virtue of orders under section 150 of the Administration Act`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the orders under section 150 are not among the sources
        WHEN JUST percentage THEN JUST (`the weekly rate of the additional pension in pounds` TIMES (1 PLUS (percentage DIVIDED BY 100)))
    ELSE JUST `the weekly rate of the additional pension in pounds`  -- unmodified, not a "no": subsection (11) increases the amount "in the case of" a pensioner whose spouse or civil partner (a) attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2016 and (b) died after attaining it; outside that case the amount stands as determined under subsection (2) (marginal reading (c) in NOTES.md)

-- (8): subsections (4) to (7) do not apply where the spouse dies on or after 9 April 2001.
-- src:1568 | (8) Nothing in subsections (4) to (7) above applies in a case where the spouse dies on or after 9 April 2001.
@ref s 48B(8) (src:1568)
GIVEN `the spouse died on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48B(8) subsections (4) to (7) are disapplied` MEANS
    `the spouse died on` AT LEAST (Date 9 4 2001)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsections (4) to (7) above applies in a case where the spouse dies on or after 9 April 2001" -- a failed "where" is read like a failed "if" (marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md)

-- (5): the condition is that the pensioner (a) is entitled (or is treated by regulations as entitled) to a widow's
-- pension by virtue of section 38 and (b) became entitled to that pension in consequence of the spouse's death.
-- (The PLAN's seam S17 words this input as "the late spouse was entitled"; the sentence is about the pensioner.)
-- src:1561 | (5) The condition is that the pensioner—
-- src:1562 | (a) is entitled (or is treated by regulations as entitled) to a widow’s pension by virtue of section 38 above, and
-- src:1563 | (b) became entitled to that pension in consequence of the spouse’s death.
@ref s 48B(5) (src:1561-1563)
GIVEN `s 38 the pensioner is entitled, or treated as entitled, to a widow's pension` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner became entitled to that pension in consequence of the spouse's death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(5) the condition is satisfied` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The condition is that the pensioner" is entitled to a widow's pension "and" became entitled to it in consequence of the spouse's death
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST `s 38 the pensioner is entitled, or treated as entitled, to a widow's pension`, JUST `the pensioner became entitled to that pension in consequence of the spouse's death`)

-- (4): a woman whose husband died before she attained pensionable age is entitled by virtue of his contributions if
-- (a) she attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and (b) the condition in subsection (5) is satisfied.
-- Subsection (8) takes the case away where the spouse died on or after 9 April 2001.
-- src:1555 | (4) A woman (“the pensioner”) whose husband died before she attained pensionable age is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of her husband if—
-- src:1556 | (a) she attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1557 | (b) the condition in subsection (5) is satisfied.
@ref s 48B(4) (src:1555-1557)
GIVEN woman IS A Person
      `her husband died before she attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 48B(5) the condition is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 48B(8) subsections (4) to (7) are disapplied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(4) the woman whose husband died before she attained pensionable age is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A woman (\"the pensioner\") whose husband died before she attained pensionable age is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of her husband if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a)); and "Nothing in subsections (4) to (7) above applies in a case where the spouse dies on or after 9 April 2001" (s 48B(8))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (NOT `s 48B(8) subsections (4) to (7) are disapplied`)
          , JUST (woman's `sex` EQUALS Woman)
          , JUST `her husband died before she attained pensionable age`
          , JUST (woman's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , `s 48B(5) the condition is satisfied`)

-- (7): the assumption is that a man is entitled to a pension by virtue of section 38 on the same terms and conditions,
-- and at the same rate, as a woman: for a man, the entitlement the same facts would give a woman.
-- src:1567 | (7) The assumption referred to in subsections (4A) and (6) above is that a man is entitled to a pension by virtue of section 38 above on the same terms and conditions, and at the same rate, as a woman.
@ref s 48B(7) (src:1567)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `s 38 the pensioner, if a woman, would be entitled to a widow's pension` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(7) the man is entitled by virtue of section 38 on the assumption` MEANS
    IF pensioner's `sex` EQUALS Man
    THEN `s 38 the pensioner, if a woman, would be entitled to a widow's pension`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the assumption is made "that a man is entitled"

-- (4A): a man whose wife died before he attained pensionable age is entitled by virtue of her contributions if (a) he
-- attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2010 but before 6 April 2016 and (b) the condition in (5) would have been
-- satisfied on the assumption in (7). Subsection (8) takes the case away where the spouse died on or after 9 April 2001.
-- src:1558 | (4A) A man (“the pensioner”) whose wife died before he attained pensionable age is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his wife if—
-- src:1559 | (a) he attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2010 but before 6 April 2016, and
-- src:1560 | (b) the condition in subsection (5) would have been satisfied on the assumption mentioned in subsection (7).
@ref s 48B(4A) (src:1558-1560)
GIVEN man IS A Person
      `his wife died before he attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 48B(5) the condition would have been satisfied on the assumption mentioned in subsection (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 48B(8) subsections (4) to (7) are disapplied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(4A) the man whose wife died before he attained pensionable age is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A man (\"the pensioner\") whose wife died before he attained pensionable age is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his wife if" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a)); and "Nothing in subsections (4) to (7) above applies in a case where the spouse dies on or after 9 April 2001" (s 48B(8))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (NOT `s 48B(8) subsections (4) to (7) are disapplied`)
          , JUST (man's `sex` EQUALS Man)
          , JUST `his wife died before he attained pensionable age`
          , JUST (man's `date of attaining pensionable age` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 2010))
          , JUST (man's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , `s 48B(5) the condition would have been satisfied on the assumption mentioned in subsection (7)`)

-- (6): a pension under (4) or (4A) is payable (a) for a woman at the same weekly rate as her widow's pension and (b) for
-- a man at the same weekly rate as the pension he would have been entitled to by virtue of section 38 on the assumption.
-- src:1564 | (6) A Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of subsection (4) or (4A) above shall be payable—
-- src:1565 | (a) where the pensioner is a woman, at the same weekly rate as her widow’s pension, and
-- src:1566 | (b) where the pensioner is a man, at the same weekly rate as that of the pension to which he would have been entitled by virtue of section 38 above on the assumption mentioned in subsection (7) below.
@ref s 48B(6) (src:1564-1566)
GIVEN `s 38 the weekly rate of that pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 48B(6) the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds` MEANS `s 38 the weekly rate of that pension in pounds`

§§ `Section 48BB: entitlement by reference to benefits under section 39A or 39B`

-- (1) and (2): a pensioner who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016, who was immediately before attaining it
-- entitled to a widowed parent's allowance in consequence of the death of the spouse or civil partner and has not
-- since married or formed a civil partnership, is entitled by virtue of the deceased's contributions at the same weekly
-- rate as the widowed parent's allowance.
-- src:1575 | (1) Subsection (2) below applies where a person (“the pensioner”) who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 —
-- src:1576 | (a) was, immediately before attaining that age, entitled to a widowed parent’s allowance in consequence of the death of his or her spouse or civil partner; and
-- src:1577 | (b) has not following that death married or formed a civil partnership.
-- src:1578 | (2) The pensioner shall be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the spouse or civil partner, which shall be payable at the same weekly rate as the widowed parent’s allowance.
@ref s 48BB(1) and (2) (src:1575-1578)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `immediately before attaining pensionable age the pensioner was entitled to a widowed parent's allowance in consequence of the death of the spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner has not following that death married or formed a civil partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48BB(2) the pensioner is entitled to a Category B retirement pension at the rate of the widowed parent's allowance` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) below applies where a person (\"the pensioner\") who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 -- (a) was, immediately before attaining that age, entitled to a widowed parent's allowance ... and (b) has not following that death married or formed a civil partnership" -- a failed "where" is read like a failed "if" (marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md)
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , JUST `immediately before attaining pensionable age the pensioner was entitled to a widowed parent's allowance in consequence of the death of the spouse or civil partner`
          , JUST `the pensioner has not following that death married or formed a civil partnership`)

-- src:1578 | (2) The pensioner shall be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the spouse or civil partner, which shall be payable at the same weekly rate as the widowed parent’s allowance.
@ref s 48BB(2), the rate (src:1578)
GIVEN `s 39A the weekly rate of the widowed parent's allowance in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 48BB(2) the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds` MEANS `s 39A the weekly rate of the widowed parent's allowance in pounds`

-- (3) and (4): a pensioner who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016, who in consequence of the death of the
-- spouse or civil partner was (i) entitled to a bereavement allowance under section 39B at any time before attaining
-- that age or (ii) entitled to a widowed parent's allowance at any time when over 45 (but not immediately before
-- attaining pensionable age), and has not since married or formed a civil partnership, is entitled by virtue of the
-- deceased's contributions. "Over the age of 45" is s 173's answer (seam K2).
-- src:1579 | (3) Subsections (4) to (10) below apply where a person (“the pensioner”) who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 —
-- src:1580 | (a) was in consequence of the death of his or her spouse or civil partner either—
-- src:1581 | (i) entitled to a bereavement allowance under section 39B (before that section was repealed) at any time prior to attaining that age, or
-- src:1582 | (ii) entitled to a widowed parent’s allowance at any time when over the age of 45 (but not immediately before attaining pensionable age); and
-- src:1583 | (b) has not following that death married or formed a civil partnership.
-- src:1584 | (4) The pensioner shall be entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the spouse or civil partner.
@ref s 48BB(3) and (4) (src:1579-1584)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `the pensioner was entitled to a bereavement allowance under section 39B at some time before attaining pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner was entitled to a widowed parent's allowance at some time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the pensioner was over 45 at that time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner was entitled to a widowed parent's allowance immediately before attaining pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner has not following that death married or formed a civil partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48BB(4) the pensioner is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the spouse or civil partner` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (4) to (10) below apply where a person (\"the pensioner\") who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 -- (a) was ... either -- (i) entitled to a bereavement allowance ... or (ii) entitled to a widowed parent's allowance at any time when over the age of 45 (but not immediately before attaining pensionable age); and (b) has not following that death married or formed a civil partnership" -- a failed "where" is read like a failed "if" (marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md)
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016))
          , `ssc3 helper any of`
                (LIST
                    JUST `the pensioner was entitled to a bereavement allowance under section 39B at some time before attaining pensionable age`
                  , `ssc3 helper all of`
                        (LIST
                            JUST `the pensioner was entitled to a widowed parent's allowance at some time`
                          , `s 173(a) the pensioner was over 45 at that time`
                          , JUST (NOT `the pensioner was entitled to a widowed parent's allowance immediately before attaining pensionable age`)))
          , JUST `the pensioner has not following that death married or formed a civil partnership`)

-- (9): "the relevant time" means (a) where the pensioner became entitled to a widowed parent's allowance in consequence
-- of the death, the time the entitlement to that allowance ended; (b) otherwise the time of the death.
-- src:1591 | (9) In subsection (8) above “the relevant time” means—
-- src:1592 | (a) where the pensioner became entitled to a widowed parent’s allowance in consequence of the death of the spouse or civil partner, the time when the pensioner’s entitlement to that allowance ended; and
-- src:1593 | (b) otherwise, the time of the spouse’s or civil partner's death.
@ref s 48BB(9) (src:1591-1593)
GIVEN `the pensioner became entitled to a widowed parent's allowance in consequence of the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the entitlement to the widowed parent's allowance ended` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 48BB(9) the relevant time` MEANS
    IF `the pensioner became entitled to a widowed parent's allowance in consequence of the death`
    THEN `the day the entitlement to the widowed parent's allowance ended`
    ELSE JUST `the day of the death`

-- (6): where the spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age, references to the tax year in which the pensioner
-- attained pensionable age are taken as references to the tax year in which the spouse or civil partner died.
-- src:1586 | (6) Where the spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age, references in the provisions of sections 44 to 45AA and 45B above and Schedule 4A below, as applied by subsection (5) above, to the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age shall be taken as references to the tax year in which the spouse or civil partner died.
@ref s 48BB(6) (src:1586)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `the spouse or civil partner died on` IS A DATE
      `the spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 48BB(6) the tax year taken as the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age` MEANS
    IF `the spouse or civil partner died under pensionable age`
    THEN `Tax year` OF (`ssc3 helper tax year of` `the spouse or civil partner died on`)
    ELSE `Tax year` OF (`ssc3 helper tax year of` (pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age`))

-- (7): where the spouse or civil partner dies after 5 October 2002, the pension under (4) is (before any reduction under
-- (8)) one half of what it would be apart from this subsection.
-- src:1587 | (7) Where the spouse or civil partner dies after 5th October 2002, the pension payable by virtue of subsection (4) above shall (before making any reduction required by subsection (8) below) be one half of the amount which it would be apart from this subsection.
@ref s 48BB(7) (src:1587)
GIVEN `the weekly rate apart from this subsection in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the spouse or civil partner died on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 48BB(7) the weekly rate before any reduction under subsection (8) in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the spouse or civil partner died on` GREATER THAN (Date 5 10 2002)
    THEN `the weekly rate apart from this subsection in pounds` DIVIDED BY 2
    ELSE `the weekly rate apart from this subsection in pounds`

-- (8): where the pensioner was under 55 at the relevant time, the weekly rate is reduced by 7 per cent. of what it would
-- be apart from this subsection, multiplied (a) by the number of years by which the pensioner's age at that time was
-- less than 55, any fraction of a year being counted as a year, or (b) by ten if that number exceeds ten.
-- "Under the age of 55" is s 173's answer (seam K2). For a pensioner who is under 55, the number of years by which the
-- age is less than 55, with a fraction counted as a year, is 55 minus the completed years of age: an age of 51 years
-- and 3 months is less than 55 by 3 years and 9 months, which counts as 4 = 55 - 51; an age of exactly 51 years is 4.
-- src:1588 | (8) Where the pensioner was under the age of 55 at the relevant time, the weekly rate of the pension shall be reduced by 7 per cent. of what it would be apart from this subsection multiplied—
-- src:1589 | (a) by the number of years by which the pensioner’s age at that time was less than 55 (any fraction of a year being counted as a year), or
-- src:1590 | (b) by ten, if that number exceeds ten.
@ref s 48BB(8) (src:1588-1590)
GIVEN `the weekly rate apart from this subsection in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `s 173(a) the pensioner was under 55 at the relevant time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner's age in completed years at the relevant time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 48BB(8) the weekly rate after the reduction in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 173(a) the pensioner was under 55 at the relevant time`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the pensioner was under the age of 55 is section 173's answer, which the caller has not given
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST `the weekly rate apart from this subsection in pounds`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the reduction is made only "Where the pensioner was under the age of 55 at the relevant time"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (`the weekly rate apart from this subsection in pounds`
              MINUS (`the weekly rate apart from this subsection in pounds` TIMES 0.07 TIMES (min 10 (55 MINUS `the pensioner's age in completed years at the relevant time`))))

-- (5): the weekly rate corresponds to the weekly rate of the additional pension determined under ss 44 to 45AA and 45B
-- and Schedules 4A and 4B as for a Category A retirement pension, subject to s 46, the rest of s 48BB and s 48C(4)
-- (the rate arrives from the caller; the reductions above and the increase below act on it).
-- src:1585 | (5) A Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of subsection (4) above shall be payable at a weekly rate corresponding to the weekly rate of the additional pension determined in accordance with the provisions of sections 44 to 45AA and 45B above and Schedules 4A and 4B below as they apply in relation to a Category A retirement pension, but subject to section 46 above and to the following provisions of this section and the modification in section 48C(4) below.
@ref s 48BB(5) (src:1585)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the additional pension determined as for a Category A retirement pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 48BB(5) the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension before the adjustments in pounds` MEANS `the weekly rate of the additional pension determined as for a Category A retirement pension in pounds`

-- (10): the amount determined under (5) to (9) is increased by the overall percentage by which, had the pension been in
-- payment from the date of the death until the pensioner attained pensionable age, the weekly rate would have been
-- increased by orders under section 150 of the Administration Act.
-- src:1594 | (10) The amount determined in accordance with subsections (5) to (9) above as the weekly rate of the pension payable to the pensioner by virtue of subsection (4) above shall be increased by such percentage as equals the overall percentage by which, had the pension been in payment as from the date of the spouse’s or civil partner's death until the date when the pensioner attained pensionable age, that weekly rate would have been increased during that period by virtue of any orders under section 150 of the Administration Act (annual up-rating of benefits).
@ref s 48BB(10) (src:1594)
GIVEN `the amount determined in accordance with subsections (5) to (9) in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the overall percentage by which the weekly rate would have been increased by virtue of orders under section 150 of the Administration Act` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 48BB(10) the weekly rate after the increase in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the overall percentage by which the weekly rate would have been increased by virtue of orders under section 150 of the Administration Act`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the orders under section 150 are not among the sources
    WHEN JUST percentage THEN JUST (`the amount determined in accordance with subsections (5) to (9) in pounds` TIMES (1 PLUS (percentage DIVIDED BY 100)))

§§ `Section 48C: Category B retirement pension: general`

-- (1): entitlement begins on the day the conditions of entitlement become satisfied and continues for life.
-- src:1596 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, a person’s entitlement to a Category B retirement pension shall begin on the day on which the conditions of entitlement become satisfied and shall continue for life.
@ref s 48C(1) (src:1596)
GIVEN `the day the conditions of entitlement become satisfied` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
      `the date of the pensioner's death` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48C(1) the entitlement to a Category B retirement pension is running on the day` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN `the day the conditions of entitlement become satisfied`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): entitlement "shall begin on the day on which the conditions of entitlement become satisfied"
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the date of the pensioner's death`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST death THEN IF day AT MOST death THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): it "shall continue for life"

-- (2): where a person would, apart from section 43(1), be entitled to both a Category A and a Category B retirement
-- pension and section 47(1) would apply to increase the Category A pension, section 47(1) applies also to the Category B
-- pension, subject to reduction or extinguishment under section 47(2) or section 46(5) of the Pensions Act.
-- src:1597 | (2) In any case where—
-- src:1598 | (a) a person would, apart from section 43(1) above, be entitled both to a Category A and to a Category B retirement pension, and
-- src:1599 | (b) section 47(1) above would apply for the increase of the Category A retirement pension,
-- src:1600 | section 47(1) above shall be taken as applying also for the increase of the Category B retirement pension, subject to reduction or extinguishment of the increase by the application of section 47(2) above or section 46(5) of the Pensions Act.
@ref s 48C(2) (src:1597-1600)
GIVEN `the person would apart from section 43(1) be entitled to both a Category A and a Category B retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 47(1) would apply for the increase of the Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48C(2) section 47(1) applies also for the increase of the Category B retirement pension` MEANS
    IF `the person would apart from section 43(1) be entitled to both a Category A and a Category B retirement pension` AND `section 47(1) would apply for the increase of the Category A retirement pension`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the extension is "in any case where" both facts hold

-- (3): where the spouse died on or before 5 October 2002, section 48B(2)(b) has effect without the words "half of".
-- src:1601 | (3) In the case of a pensioner whose spouse died on or before 5th October 2002, section 48B(2)(b) above shall have effect with the omission of the words “half of”.
@ref s 48C(3) (src:1601)
GIVEN `the spouse died on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48C(3) the words "half of" are omitted from section 48B(2)(b)` MEANS
    `the spouse died on` AT MOST (Date 5 10 2002)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a pensioner whose spouse died on or before 5th October 2002 ... shall have effect with the omission" -- a failed "in the case of" is read like a failed "if" (marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md)

-- (4): in the application of ss 44 to 45B and Schedules 4A and 4B by virtue of s 48B(2) or 48BB(5), references to the
-- pensioner are taken as references to the spouse or civil partner.
-- src:1602 | (4) In the application of the provisions of sections 44 to 45B above and Schedules 4A and 4B below by virtue of sections ... 48B(2) or 48BB(5) above, references in those provisions to the pensioner shall be taken as references to the spouse or civil partner.
@ref s 48C(4) (src:1602)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `spouse or civil partner` IS A Person
      `the provisions are applied by virtue of section 48B(2) or 48BB(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Person
`s 48C(4) the person to whom a reference to the pensioner is taken to refer` MEANS
    IF `the provisions are applied by virtue of section 48B(2) or 48BB(5)`
    THEN JUST `spouse or civil partner`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the reading is "in the application of the provisions ... by virtue of sections ... 48B(2) or 48BB(5)"
